!! Capturing a fleeting note

Click ''+ Note'' in the topbar. Type ''typescript-tips'' and submit. A new tiddler appears at `knowledge/inbox/typescript-tips` with body:

```
\context knowledge

```

…and `kn.tier=fleeting`.

!! Linking by short ref

In a note titled `knowledge/topics/programming/typescript/Foo`, write:

```
\context knowledge

See also [[Bar]] for details, or [[topics/python/Snake]] for the cousin language.
```

The namespace walk-up resolves `[[Bar]]` against the source's path: tries `knowledge/topics/programming/typescript/Bar`, then `knowledge/topics/programming/Bar`, then `knowledge/topics/Bar`, etc. The absolute path `topics/python/Snake` is not absolute (no leading `/`) — it walks up too: `knowledge/topics/programming/typescript/topics/python/Snake` (no), then `…/programming/topics/python/Snake` (no), then `…/topics/topics/python/Snake` (no), then `…/topics/python/Snake` (yes, if it exists).

!! Cross-app linking

In an orga app meeting note (e.g. `orga/meetings/2026-04-30/notes`), write:

```
Discussion ref: [[kn/topics/programming/typescript/Foo]]
```

The starter mount `kn → knowledge` rewrites the prefix, and the link resolves to `knowledge/topics/programming/typescript/Foo`.

!! Topic index page

Create a tiddler `knowledge/topics/typescript/index` summarising the topic. From any note in that tree (or anywhere with the right context), write `[[knowledge/topics/typescript/_index]]` — the `_index` pseudo expands to `index` (or `README`) at that prefix.

!! Promote a note

In Note view, click the tier pill. It cycles `fleeting → developing → evergreen → fleeting`. Tier counts on Home and the sidebar update immediately.

